{"url": "https://www.gc.cuny.edu/mathematics/admissions-and-aid", "final_url": "https://www.gc.cuny.edu/mathematics/admissions-and-aid", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "SKIP TO MAIN CONTENT\nSKIP TO MAIN SITE NAVIGATION\nCUNY Home\nThe Graduate Center, CUNY Home\nINFORMATION FOR\nLIBRARY\nDIRECTORY\nGIVING\nAPPLY\nATTEND AN EVENT\nSEARCH\nACADEMICS\nADMISSIONS AND AID\nRESEARCH AND FACULTY\nSTUDENT LIFE\nNEWS AND EVENTS\nABOUT\nCUNY Home\nThe Graduate Center, CUNY Home\nAPPLY\nATTEND AN EVENT\nMENU\nSearch Site\nSEARCH\nACADEMICS\nADMISSIONS AND AID\nRESEARCH AND FACULTY\nSTUDENT LIFE\nNEWS AND EVENTS\nABOUT\nINFORMATION FOR\nLIBRARY\nDIRECTORY\nGIVING\nMATHEMATICS ADMISSIONS AND AID\nADMISSIONS AND AID\nMORE IN MATHEMATICS\nCURRICULUM AND DEGREE INFORMATION\nCourses\nPrevious Course Schedules\nQualifying Examinations\nADMISSIONS AND AID\nFACULTY\nFaculty by Field\nFaculty Distinctions\nFaculty Books\nPostdocs\nSEMINARS AND EVENTS\nSeminars\nEvents\nOur scholars in action\nPROGRAM NEWS\nALUMNI\nCURRENT STUDENTS\nSTUDENT RESOURCES\nForms and Procedures\nMath Links\nCONTACT US\nSUPPORT US\nPROSPECTIVE STUDENTS ARE INVITED TO MATHFEST 2024\nTuesday, November 12, 2024 | 10 a.m. - 2:30 p.m.\nLocated in-person and remote via Zoom.\nView event details\nEvent flyer\nProspective students to the CUNY Graduate Center's Ph.D. program in Mathematics should review the information below, and visit the Office of Admissions and Office of Fellowships and Financial Aid.\nAdmissions Deadline:\nJanuary 1 for fall enrollment\nCandidates should have a strong background and high-performance marks in the foundational areas of mathematics: Topology, Algebra, Real Analysis, and Complex Analysis. Candidates should have experience performing research in mathematics and understands what mathematical research entails.\nApplications to the Mathematics program are handled through the CUNY Graduate Center's Office of Admissions, please visit their How to Apply page:\nLEARN MORE OR APPLY ONLINE\nFELLOWSHIPS AND FINANCIAL AID\nCLICK TO OPEN\nINSTITUTIONAL AID\nEvery applicant to the Graduate Center\u2019s doctoral programs will automatically be considered for five-year institutional funding packages. The aid we offer \u2014 including fellowships, tuition awards, and assistantships \u2014 is based on merit.\nLearn more about institutional aid for doctoral students \u00bb\nCLICK TO OPEN\nFEDERAL AID\nFederal aid for doctoral students includes:\nNeed-based Federal Aid\nFederal Work-Study\nNon-need-based Federal Direct Loans\nCLICK TO OPEN\nSUPPORT FOR UNDERREPRESENTED GROUPS\nAdditional funding may be available to doctoral students from underrepresented populations through offerings from the Office of Educational Opportunity and Diversity, including several fellowships and the CUNY Pipeline Program.\nLearn more about funding opportunities from OEOD \u00bb\nTUITION AND FEES\nTuition rates for doctoral programs at the Graduate Center are based on a student's \u201clevel,\u201d which is determined by a combination of the number of graduate credits completed (including, in the case of transfer students, credits accepted by the student's degree program and the Registrar) and specific academic accomplishments.\nThe fee structure is also affected by a student\u2019s resident status.\nSee current doctoral tuition rates \u00bb\nCLICK TO OPEN\nSTUDENT ACTIVITY FEE\nEach student will be billed for a Graduate School student activities fee, a University student senate fee, a University consolidated services fee and a technology fee. These fees are not refundable.\nJOIN US\nWE BELIEVE THAT KNOWLEDGE IS A PUBLIC GOOD\nAPPLY\nREQUEST INFO\nATTEND AN EVENT\nCUNY Home\nCUNY GRADUATE CENTER\n365 FIFTH AVENUE\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n+1 877-428-6942\n+1 212-817-7000\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nYouTube\nBluesky\nFACULTY & STUDENTS\nCUNYfirst\nBrightspace\nEmail\nABOUT\nCareers\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nBuilding Access\nRESOURCES\nT